## 1. Deduplication (SYNTHETIC streams, ground truth by construction)

population: 1050 events = 500 origins + 300 duplicates + 250 near-miss negatives

### 1.1 Scheme A — exact `event_id` only (baseline)

| metric | value |
|---|---|
| duplicates found (TP) | 150 |
| false merges (FP) | 0 |
| missed duplicates (FN) | 150 |
| precision | 1.0000 |
| recall | 0.5000 |
| false-merge rate FP/(TP+FP) | 0.0000 |
| undetected-duplicate rate FN/(TP+FN) | 0.5000 |

Ground truth is built in, and the population contains one class that is
**undecidable by content** (D1: same command text, same session, inside the
window — a human double-tap or a genuine double-report). D1 merges are
reported in their own column and are NOT counted as false positives, because
no content-based scheme can separate them. Every other negative is decidable.

### 1.2 Scheme B — semantic fingerprint, parameter sweep

key = `type_class | session? | subject | ts_bucket`; `session?` is `-`
unless `require_same_session`. Every row is a full re-run of the stream.
precision is TP/(TP+decidable FP); `D1 merged` is the irreducible residue.

